  "query_preview": "..\nA minor trade-wind trough within a retreating trade-wind surge is\nexpected to bring scattered showers to the region tonight. Guam and \nRota may see showers earlier than Saipan and Tinian, but satellite \ntrends suggest this difference to not be significant enough for a \nzone split. Model time heights show dry mid- and upper-level air to \ncontinue, so thunderstorms are not a concern for tonight. A ridge\nwill fill in afterwards, so showers decrease to isolated Wednesday \nthrough Thanksgiving Day. Then, a wetter pattern with thunderstorm\npotential is possible Thursday night through the weekend as a\nweakening upper-level low and surface troughing interact near the \nregion. Gusts may reach up to 30 mph near heavier showers as the \ntrade-wind surge re-develops as well. As of now, scattered showers\ntop out at 40 percent, so this will continue to be monitored over the\nnext few periods.",
